# bgp-labeled-1 decoding test - Labeled IPv4 Unicast NLRI via ze bgp decode
# Tests labeled unicast 10.0.0.0/8 with label=100 per RFC 8277 Section 2.2
#
# Wire bytes breakdown:
# 20 = prefix length 32 bits (24 label + 8 prefix)
# 00 06 41 = label 100 (value << 4 | S-bit=1)
# Each stack member is published as the pair [label, entry]: the 20-bit value
# a reader matches on, and the 3-octet entry it came from, which carries the
# traffic class and the bottom-of-stack bit. 0x000641 is 1601.
# 0A = 10 (10.0.0.0/8)
stdin=payload:hex=200006410A
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze bgp decode --json --nlri ipv4/mpls-label -:stdin=payload
expect=json:json={"labels":[[100,1601]],"prefix":"10.0.0.0/8"}
